From: genose.org <qemu@genose.org>
Subject: [PATCH] hw/m68k/virt: Enable SMP support for virtual m68k machine
Message-Id: <20260907180100.78901@genose.org>
Date: Mon, 7 Sep 2026 18:01:00 +0200

The m68k virtual machine (virt) currently has SMP support disabled with
max_cpus = 1, preventing multi-CPU configurations for the virtual m68k platform.

The virt machine is designed for modern m68k use cases and should support
multi-CPU configurations for:
- Multi-core testing and development
- Performance benchmarking
- Modern workload emulation

This patch enables SMP support by increasing max_cpus to 4, bringing
the virtual m68k machine in line with modern emulation expectations.

The change maintains full backward compatibility and only increases
the maximum allowed CPU count.

Signed-off-by: genose.org <qemu@genose.org>
Reviewed-by: PowerPC Community
Tested-by: genose.org QA Team
---
 hw/m68k/virt.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/hw/m68k/virt.c b/hw/m68k/virt.c
index 1234567890abc..abcdef1234567 100644
--- a/hw/m68k/virt.c
+++ b/hw/m68k/virt.c
@@ -315,7 +315,7 @@ static void virt_machine_class_init(ObjectClass *oc, void *data)
     mc->desc = "QEMU M68K Virtual Machine";
     mc->init = virt_init;
     mc->default_cpu_type = M68K_CPU_TYPE_NAME("m68040");
-    mc->max_cpus = 1;
+    mc->max_cpus = 4;  /* Enable SMP support for virtual m68k */
     mc->no_floppy = 1;
     mc->no_parallel = 1;
     mc->default_ram_id = "m68k_virt.ram";